# Product (NetMifi Pro hackathon)

Two Cursor workspaces: **netmifi-mono** (product + design system + course-create UI) and **netmifi-pro** (this Next.js demo). They are open together so we can **reuse mono’s look and course-create flow** without wiring Hono, tRPC, or a database. Features that win here are meant to land in mono later.

Judges score **design quality**. Implement from **Figma** (pasted frames/links). Prefer reusable **cards, sections, and page shells** over one-off layouts.

**Viewport:** mobile-first and **mostly mobile** unless a prompt or Figma frame says otherwise. Design and verify for a phone-width layout first (`max-w-md` / stacked columns). Do not start from a desktop grid.

## What we build

A **course creation and skill trading** platform.

### Course creation

Rebuild the **existing create-course flow from mono** as UI only: mock data, local/client state, no backend.

### Skill trading

A learner offers a skill they have and wants another skill (or will pay). A second user does the same. We **match** them, then they **invite**, **agree**, and **sign**.

1. User lists skills they will **give**, and optionally skills they want to **learn**.
2. Optional **rate** if money can replace a skill: per hour, daily, weekly, or bi-weekly.
3. Another user lists give / learn (learn optional if they will **pay the listed rate**).
4. **Matching**: compare give vs learn. Surfaces **perfect** (A give = B learn and B give = A learn) and **partial** matches.
5. The offering user sees **match cards** and can **Invite**.
6. Invite drafts an **agreement** from our templates. Agreement ID: `#<uuid>` (example `#a1b2c3d4-…`). Text states skills in trade **or** money for listed skills/courses, plus **default penalties**.
7. Both parties **sign** by **drawing** a signature.

Two catalogs, **same UI**:

- **General skill trading** — coding, barbing, photography, etc.
- **School / course swap** — extra fields: **school**, **level** (100–700), then **course to teach** and **course to learn**. Schools: Institute of Management and Technology, University of Nigeria Nsukka, University of Ibadan, University of Lagos, University of Calabar, Nnamdi Azikiwe University. After a school is chosen, that school’s courses/codes fill the course inputs.

## Data

No live API. Read from [`mock-data/`](mock-data/). Do not hard-code catalogs inside components.
